module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_carrier_body_under_a_scalar_declared_return_is_accepted

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data a_carrier_body_under_a_scalar_declared_return_is_accepted: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_carrier_body_under_a_scalar_declared_return_is_accepted" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a function declares a SCALAR (kernel) return -- here `-> String` -- and its body produces a CARRIER Variant (here v2.std.diagnostic.Outcome<String>, a Result-like Accepted/Rejected sum), and the program is Accepted. HARM: silent wrongness at the compiler floor. The consumer reads the DECLARATION, treats the value as the scalar, and feeds it to a position typed by the scalar or its refined alias (here a github.actions RunStep `run:` field typed NonEmptyStr = String where string_non_empty). Nothing refuses at the declaration, so the value fails later, inside a primitive cast, as `TypeError { msg: \"cannot cast Outcome (runtime carrier Variant) to NonEmptyStr\" }` -- a message that names neither the lying declaration nor the site that trusted it.",

    "HOW IT SURFACED (zesty-ram-689, gunbc typed-refusal lane, 2026-11-18; VERIFIED BY EXECUTION, one reader). The run-step emitter v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit was retyped to return Outcome<String> from a String that previously carried an in-band sentinel. A wrapper still declared `-> String` whose body's final expression forwards such an emitter call. `gunbc run --entry dag/gunbc/drift_watch_workflow.dag --function expected_drift_watch_workflow_yml` reported `phase=closure_typecheck ms=0` (zero blocking errors across the 889-module closure) and then aborted in evaluation with the cast message above. Bisecting by replacing the workflow builder with a literal still aborted -- the carrier is produced on an upstream path whose consumer trusts the wrapper's String declaration. The positive control (the same workflow before the emitter retype) renders, so the abort is attributable to the carrier reaching the refined field, not to the bisect edits.",

    "WHY THE EXISTING WALL MISSES IT. v1.compiler.infer DOES have a declared-return-vs-body conformance wall (explicit_return_conformance_note, reusing declared_type_conformance_diags), and it is not idle: it refuses a String trailing expression under `-> Int`. But its declared scope is gated on where 'the declared and produced SHAPES DIFFER', and it names 'generic record instantiation' and 'post-substitution generic field access' as SEPARATE LANES not yet admitted. The drift here enters through a CALLEE'S DECLARED RETURN that the wrapper trusts: the wrapper's body final expression is a call whose own declaration says String, so at the wrapper the inferred body type is String and conforms -- while at the callee, the produced carrier under the scalar declaration is the unjoined pair. The generalisation of the generic row's observation -- 'every consumer reads the DECLARATION, passes the value into a parameter typed A, and the mismatch surfaces inside a callee that names neither the declaration nor the drift' -- is exactly this: the lie lives one declaration away from where it is judged.",

    "DISTINCT FROM ITS NEIGHBOURS. declared_return_disagrees_with_the_generic_it_returns is a carrier whose GENERIC ARGUMENT drifts (`F<A>` declared against `F<B>` produced); here the carrier is not a drifted instantiation but a WHOLE Result-like Variant whose declared return is a bare scalar -- there is no type parameter that is 'wrong', the whole carrier is un-admitted. list_typed_value_element_mismatch_admitted is a List<T> into List<U> (both container applications, element axes distinct); here one side is a kernel scalar and the other a named sum. product_value_at_a_scalar_formal_is_accepted is a product at a scalar FORMAL; this is a carrier at a scalar DECLARED RETURN of the producer, the producer end rather than the consumer end.",

    "THE LOUD PATH (rung-1 shape, cast route). Where the produced carrier reaches a primitive cast -- a github.actions RunStep `run:` field typed NonEmptyStr -- it aborts at evaluation with `TypeError { msg: \"cannot cast Outcome (runtime carrier Variant) to NonEmptyStr\" }`: a typed runtime abort with containment (it names the carrier and the refined target) but no locality (it does not name the declaration that lied). That route alone would be a rung-1 mitigatable failure.",

    "THE SILENT PATH (below the ladder -- and it is the route that sets the class). The SAME carrier, handed to a consumer that DECLARES the scalar and then MATCHES it rather than casts it, does not abort. The type checker's floor defect accepts an Outcome<Step> where a Step is declared, so passing one straight to a scalar-declared reader is ACCEPTED at the call, the RunStep match simply misses, and a plausible default -- the empty string -- comes out silently, with no diagnostic and no committed-versus-refused signal. The witnesses that read the retyped run-step producers record exactly this and are the reason they unwrap first: `step_name_of`/`step_if_of` (test.claim.fleet.fleet_converge_hostname_converge_emitter_witness) and `probe_step_if_of` (test.claim.host.boot_medium_reader_probe_witness) each unwrap the accepted Step before handing it to a Step-declared reader, precisely because handing the carrier over silently misses rather than erroring. The formal-drift that carries the value into the Step-typed parameter is taxonomically the neighbour `product_value_at_a_scalar_formal_is_accepted`; it is recorded HERE because it is the consumer-side manifestation of THIS drift -- a carrier produced under a scalar declared return, trusted by a consumer that reads the declaration -- and a class's rung is the minimum across its in-scope paths.",

    "RUNG: UNREAD, not 1. gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder fixes a class's rung at the MINIMUM across its in-scope paths and states 'Silent wrongness is not a rung: it is below the ladder and forbidden outright.' Because the silent match-miss route is in scope, the rung cannot be ranked 1 on the strength of the loud cast route; the structured `rung:` field is RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated } and these receipts do not contradict it. Re-ranking this class -- loud or silent -- first requires naming the blocker class that makes the silent route a typed refusal rather than a missing-match-arm default.",

    "PRODUCTION REACHABILITY. As of this change the silent route is reached only by witness readers, not by production: the emitter retype (v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit and every *_invoke / *_step / *_job / workflow_of wrapper) was done in one motion per gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration, so no committed production consumer now hands an Outcome to a scalar-declared Step or String position -- the byte-identical render of every committed workflow is the execution proof that the production path is type-correct end to end. The capability gap is nonetheless unchanged: a single still-String production wrapper introduced later would be invisible to the type checker and reach the SAME silent match-miss route at its first consumer, which is why the NEXT TRIGGER below is a named capability rather than a review-only note.",

    "CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed. Both the declared scalar and the body's produced carrier are in hand at the same grain at the declaration boundary, so a checker that compares a declared scalar return against the body's inferred type, admitting a carrier Variant versus a kernel/refined scalar as a refused pair, makes no Accepted program contain it. Anything below 3 on this pair is a correctness gap, not a ceiling.",

    "NEXT TRIGGER, named as the CAPABILITY: extend the v1.compiler.infer declared-return conformance wall so a CARRIER Variant produced under a SCALAR or REFINED-SCALAR declared return is refused at the declaration, joining the produced carrier to the declared scalar across a callee whose declaration the consumer trusts; the wall must refuse BOTH consumer manifestations -- the primitive cast (loud abort) and a carrier reaching a scalar-declared FORMAL that is then matched (silent missing-arm default). Until that class is admitted this row is a review discipline: when retyping a producer from a sentinel String to a carrier, retype EVERY wrapper on the path in the same change (DESIGN replacement_migration), because a single still-String wrapper is invisible to the type checker and surfaces only when a workflow executes -- and even then it can surface LOUDLY (a cast abort) or SILENTLY (a scalar-declared match that misses and yields a plausible default), so the review discipline must inspect both the cast sites and the scalar-declared readers on the path.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit", decl_name: "gunbc_run_step_script", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.diagnostic", decl_name: "Outcome", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "extdeps.github.actions", decl_name: "RunStep", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "explicit_return_conformance_note", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "declared_type_conformance_diags", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.declared_return_disagrees_with_the_generic_it_returns", decl_name: "declared_return_disagrees_with_the_generic_it_returns", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.list_typed_value_element_mismatch_admitted", decl_name: "list_typed_value_element_mismatch_admitted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.fleet.fleet_converge_hostname_converge_emitter_witness", decl_name: "step_name_of", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.host.boot_medium_reader_probe_witness", decl_name: "probe_step_if_of", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
